Negative control for the empty state living INSIDE the table (C9).

Withdraws the table whenever the list is empty, so the empty message renders in
place of the frame and the headers disappear — "no results found" replacing the
table instead of feeling in it.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the empty-state specs — the headers stay and the message renders in the
table body.

diff --git a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue
--- a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue
+++ b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue
@@ -141,7 +141,10 @@
 
     <!-- The table is the FRAME: its headers stay through every state, and each
          state is drawn inside its body rather than in place of it (C8/C9). -->
-    <Table v-else-if="meta.hasTable" :class="styles.listSurface.table">
+    <Table
+      v-else-if="meta.hasTable && !meta.isEmpty"
+      :class="styles.listSurface.table"
+    >
       <TableHeader>
         <TableRow
           v-for="headerGroup in vueTable.getHeaderGroups()"
